{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795829426,"nonce":"dj0x/xg67g4fw/+znM7YJWEVCNw=","title":"A CSS skew inside transform is applied twice","message":"transform: skewX(10deg) draws twice the skew: the resting transform of a node has 2 * tan(10deg) in its shear element. The same holds for skewY and skew(x, y).\n\nparse_transform_with_3d puts the skew into the affine of style.transform and also sets style.skew_x / skew_y. apply_element_style_to_props then composes skew_x / skew_y onto the transform again.\n\nThe separate fields are needed: keyframes read them, and the skew-x / skew-y properties set only them. So the style has to say whether its transform already holds the skew.\n\nReproducer: a node with class x, the sheet \".x { transform: skewX(10deg) }\", then read props.transform after apply_all_stylesheet_styles.","files":null}]}